                                                inserted a <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;p&gt;</fo:inline> element containing explanatory
                                                text, and then opened a new <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;ul&gt;</fo:inline> element to continue the list.
                                                Because the paragraph sits outside both list
                                                elements, it has no <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;li&gt;</fo:inline> markup, even though it appears
                                                visually between two bullets.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
