                                        URL Rather than a Local Package Reference</fo:inline></fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                
                                <fo:block-container space-after="0" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0.5em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">Consider an HTML
                                        document where the author has referenced an image using an
                                        absolute external</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="1em" space-before="1em" role="Sect"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">
                                        <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">Consider an
                                            HTML document where the author has referenced an image
                                            using an absolute external URL (for example, hosted on a
                                            separate website or CDN) instead of a relative path to a
                                            file included in the HTML package. Because the image
                                            file is not part of the submitted package, the converter
                                            cannot extract it.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                        <fo:block>
                                            <fo:table-and-caption border-collapse="collapse" id="d689e12006" space-before="1em" space-after="1em"><fo:table-caption start-indent="0" end-indent="0" keep-with-next="always"><fo:block-container page-break-after="avoid" font-weight="bold" margin-top="0.5em" text-align="left"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0"><fo:inline>Table<fo:inline> 60</fo:inline><fo:inline>. </fo:inline></fo:inline><fo:inline><fo:inline>Image linked via external
