                                                  </fo:table-body></fo:table></fo:table-and-caption>
                                                </fo:block>
                                                <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0"><fo:inline font-weight="bold">Result:</fo:inline> The converter maps the <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;figure&gt;</fo:inline> and <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;figcaption&gt;</fo:inline> inside the <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;li&gt;</fo:inline> to a <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;fig&gt;</fo:inline> structure, placed inside <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;step&gt;&lt;info&gt;</fo:inline>, not inside <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;cmd&gt;</fo:inline>. The task body remains a
                                                  single contiguous <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;steps&gt;</fo:inline> block.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                            </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                        </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    </fo:block>
                                </fo:block>
                                <fo:block role="Sect" id="unique_107" xml:lang="en-us" chfox:nd-id="_Toc235450438">
                                    <fo:block-container page-break-after="avoid" font-size="1.4em" space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em" role="H3" id="ariaid-title107"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0"><fo:inline background-color="transparent" color="transparent" font-size="0px" max-width="2px" vertical-align="super" id="d689e17085"/><fo:inline background-color="transparent" color="transparent" font-size="0px" max-width="2px" vertical-align="super" id="d689e17089"/><fo:inline background-color="transparent" color="transparent" font-size="0px" max-width="2px" vertical-align="super" id="d689e17093"/><fo:inline>Reference Topic</fo:inline></fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">
                                        <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0.5em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">A reference
                                            section is recognized by a noun-phrase heading
                                            containing a lookup keyword such as</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                        <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">A reference
                                            section is recognized by a noun-phrase heading
                                            containing a lookup keyword such as "Supported File
                                            Formats," "Error Codes," or "API Parameters," paired
                                            with a table or parameter list as the dominant body
                                            structure. The heading keyword is the primary
                                            classification signal. A section containing only a table
                                            but no lookup keyword in the heading may be classified
                                            as Concept or Generic depending on the surrounding
                                            context.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                        <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">When these
                                            signals align, the converter generates a <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;reference&gt;</fo:inline> element with <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;refbody&gt;</fo:inline>. The opening paragraph maps
                                            to <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;shortdesc&gt;</fo:inline>. Any introductory prose
                                            appearing before the first table is wrapped in a <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;section&gt;</fo:inline> element inside <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;refbody&gt;</fo:inline> rather than placed directly
                                            in <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;refbody&gt;</fo:inline>. A 2-column table in a
                                            section whose heading contains an API keyword such as
                                            "API," "parameters," "fields," or "attributes" maps to
                                                <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;properties&gt;</fo:inline>. The same 2-column table
                                            in a reference section without an API keyword maps to
                                                <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;simpletable&gt;</fo:inline>.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                        <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">The following
                                            scenarios demonstrate how different HTML reference
                                            patterns are interpreted during HTML-to-DITA
                                            conversion:</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    <fo:block role="Sect" id="unique_108" xml:lang="en-us" chfox:nd-id="_headingh3e98s1blw8h4">
                                        <fo:block-container page-break-after="avoid" font-size="1.4em" space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em" role="H4" id="ariaid-title108"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0"><fo:inline>Scenario 1 — Standard Multi -
                                                Column Table Reference</fo:inline></fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                        
                                        <fo:block-container space-after="0" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">
                                            <fo:block-container space-after="1em" space-before="1em" role="Sect" id="unique_108_Connect_42_sec_d65e7" chfox:nd-id="sec_d65e7"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">
                                                <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">A
                                                  section titled "Printer Configuration Parameters"
                                                  contains a brief introductory sentence and a
                                                  multi-column table of configuration settings. The
                                                  heading contains the keyword "Parameters", and a
                                                  lookup table dominates the body.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                                <fo:block>
                                                  <fo:table-and-caption border-collapse="collapse" id="d689e17159" space-before="1em" space-after="1em"><fo:table-caption start-indent="0" end-indent="0" keep-with-next="always"><fo:block-container page-break-after="avoid" font-weight="bold" margin-top="0.5em" text-align="left"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0"><fo:inline>Table<fo:inline> 93</fo:inline><fo:inline>. </fo:inline></fo:inline><fo:inline><fo:inline>Standard multi-column table
                                                  reference</fo:inline></fo:inline></fo:block></fo:block-container></fo:table-caption><fo:table-caption-for-next-page start-indent="0" end-indent="0" keep-with-next="always"><fo:block-container page-break-after="avoid" font-weight="bold" margin-top="0.5em" text-align="left"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0"><fo:inline>Table<fo:inline> 93</fo:inline><fo:inline>. </fo:inline></fo:inline><fo:inline><fo:inline>Standard multi-column table
                                                  reference</fo:inline></fo:inline><fo:inline> (continued)</fo:inline></fo:block></fo:block-container></fo:table-caption-for-next-page><fo:table relative-align="baseline" chfox:html-table-width-policy="yes" table-layout="auto" border-bottom-color="black" border-bottom-style="solid" border-bottom-width="1px" border-left-color="black" border-left-style="solid" border-left-width="1px" margin-left="0" border-right-color="black" border-right-style="solid" border-right-width="1px" margin-right="0" border-top-color="black" border-top-style="solid" border-top-width="1px" hyphenate="true" space-before="0" space-after="0"><fo:table-column/><fo:table-column/><fo:table-header font-weight="bold" text-align="center" display-align="center">
