                                <fo:block role="Sect" id="unique_110" xml:lang="en-us" chfox:nd-id="_Toc235450439">
                                    <fo:block-container page-break-after="avoid" font-size="1.4em" space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em" role="H3" id="ariaid-title110"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0"><fo:inline background-color="transparent" color="transparent" font-size="0px" max-width="2px" vertical-align="super" id="d689e17375"/><fo:inline background-color="transparent" color="transparent" font-size="0px" max-width="2px" vertical-align="super" id="d689e17379"/><fo:inline background-color="transparent" color="transparent" font-size="0px" max-width="2px" vertical-align="super" id="d689e17383"/><fo:inline>Troubleshooting Topic</fo:inline></fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">
                                        <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0.5em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">A
                                            troubleshooting section is recognized by a
                                            problem-oriented heading such as "The Printer Does
                                            Not</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                        <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">A
                                            troubleshooting section is recognized by a
                                            problem-oriented heading such as "The Printer Does Not
                                            Power On" or "Print Jobs Fail to Complete," paired with
                                            a body that presents a condition, a cause, and a
                                            corrective action. The converter looks for bold labels
                                            in the form <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">
                                                <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Cause:</fo:inline>
                                            </fo:inline> and <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">
                                                <fo:inline font-weight="bold">Remedy:</fo:inline>
                                            </fo:inline> in the body. Both the heading and the body
                                            labels must be present. A problem-oriented heading
                                            without cause and remedy labels causes the converter to
                                            classify the section as Task or Generic depending on the
                                            body structure.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                        <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">When these
                                            signals align, the converter generates a <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;troubleshooting&gt;</fo:inline> element with <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;troublebody&gt;</fo:inline>. The problem heading
                                            maps to <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;title&gt;</fo:inline> and the condition text maps to
                                                <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;condition&gt;</fo:inline>. Each cause label and its
                                            associated text maps to <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;cause&gt;</fo:inline> inside a <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;troubleSolution&gt;</fo:inline> block. Each remedy
                                            label and its associated steps maps to <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;remedy&gt;</fo:inline> inside the same <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;troubleSolution&gt;</fo:inline> block, with each
                                                <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;li&gt;</fo:inline> mapping to <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;step&gt;&lt;cmd&gt;</fo:inline>. When a section
                                            contains multiple cause-and-remedy pairs, the converter
                                            generates one <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;condition&gt;</fo:inline> at the top of <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;troublebody&gt;</fo:inline> and a separate <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;troubleSolution&gt;</fo:inline> for each pair. The
                                            condition is not repeated for each solution.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                        <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">The following
                                            scenarios demonstrate how different HTML troubleshooting
                                            patterns are interpreted during HTML-to-DITA
                                            conversion:</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    <fo:block role="Sect" id="unique_111" xml:lang="en-us" chfox:nd-id="_headinghp10c6clurdgw">
                                        <fo:block-container page-break-after="avoid" font-size="1.4em" space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em" role="H4" id="ariaid-title111"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0"><fo:inline background-color="transparent" color="transparent" font-size="0px" max-width="2px" vertical-align="super" id="d689e17499"/><fo:inline background-color="transparent" color="transparent" font-size="0px" max-width="2px" vertical-align="super" id="d689e17503"/><fo:inline background-color="transparent" color="transparent" font-size="0px" max-width="2px" vertical-align="super" id="d689e17507"/><fo:inline>Scenario 1 — Clearly defined
                                                problem, cause and remedy</fo:inline></fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                        
                                        <fo:block-container space-after="0" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">
                                            <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0.5em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">Consider an HTML document
                                                containing a troubleshooting section with a clearly
                                                defined problem, its cause,</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                            <fo:block-container space-after="1em" space-before="1em" role="Sect"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">
                                                <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">Consider
                                                  an HTML document containing a troubleshooting
                                                  section with a clearly defined problem, its cause,
                                                  and the corresponding remedy. The following
                                                  example shows how the converter transforms this
                                                  structure into a DITA <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;troubleshooting&gt;</fo:inline> topic.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                                <fo:block>
                                                  <fo:table-and-caption border-collapse="collapse" id="d689e17527" space-before="1em" space-after="1em"><fo:table-caption start-indent="0" end-indent="0" keep-with-next="always"><fo:block-container page-break-after="avoid" font-weight="bold" margin-top="0.5em" text-align="left"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0"><fo:inline>Table<fo:inline> 95</fo:inline><fo:inline>. </fo:inline></fo:inline><fo:inline><fo:inline>Troubleshooting: problem,
                                                  cause,
                                                  remedy</fo:inline></fo:inline></fo:block></fo:block-container></fo:table-caption><fo:table-caption-for-next-page start-indent="0" end-indent="0" keep-with-next="always"><fo:block-container page-break-after="avoid" font-weight="bold" margin-top="0.5em" text-align="left"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0"><fo:inline>Table<fo:inline> 95</fo:inline><fo:inline>. </fo:inline></fo:inline><fo:inline><fo:inline>Troubleshooting: problem,
