                                </fo:block>
                                <fo:block role="Sect" id="unique_113" xml:lang="en-us" chfox:nd-id="_Toc235450440">
                                    <fo:block-container page-break-after="avoid" font-size="1.4em" space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em" role="H3" id="ariaid-title113"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0"><fo:inline background-color="transparent" color="transparent" font-size="0px" max-width="2px" vertical-align="super" id="d689e17774"/><fo:inline background-color="transparent" color="transparent" font-size="0px" max-width="2px" vertical-align="super" id="d689e17778"/><fo:inline background-color="transparent" color="transparent" font-size="0px" max-width="2px" vertical-align="super" id="d689e17782"/><fo:inline>Generic Topic</fo:inline></fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    
                                    <fo:block-container space-after="0" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">
                                        <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0.5em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">A Generic
                                            topic is the converter's fallback classification when
                                            the heading and body content together</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                        <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">A Generic
                                            topic is the converter's fallback classification when
                                            the heading and body content together do not provide
                                            sufficient signals to identify a Concept, Task,
                                            Reference, or Troubleshooting pattern. The most common
                                            triggers are a descriptive heading followed only by a
                                                <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;ul&gt;</fo:inline> list, mixed body content where no
                                            single element type is dominant, a heading verb and body
                                            structure that conflict, or a section with no
                                            introductory paragraph and no table or ordered list. A
                                                <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;ul&gt;</fo:inline> list on its own never triggers
                                            task classification — task classification requires both
                                            an imperative heading and an <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;ol&gt;</fo:inline> as the primary body content.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                        <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">When Generic
                                            classification is assigned, the converter generates a
                                            standard <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;topic&gt;</fo:inline> element with <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;body&gt;</fo:inline>. All supported HTML elements
                                            are mapped in document order without applying the
                                            specialized structures associated with other topic
                                            types. When no introductory paragraph is present, the
                                            converter writes an empty <fo:inline background-color="rgb(238 , 238 , 238)" color="rgb(128 , 0 , 0)" font-family="monospace" font-size="0.8em" role="Code" padding-bottom="2px" padding-left="0" padding-right="0" padding-top="2px">&lt;shortdesc&gt;</fo:inline> and flags it at WARNING
                                            severity in the conversion report. Generic topics are
                                            also flagged as candidates for manual reclassification
                                            if the content appears to match a more specific topic
                                            type.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                        <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">The following
                                            scenarios demonstrate how different HTML patterns result
                                            in Generic classification during HTML-to-DITA
                                            conversion:</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    </fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                    <fo:block role="Sect" id="unique_114" xml:lang="en-us" chfox:nd-id="_headinghem4752qtfk5x">
                                        <fo:block-container page-break-after="avoid" font-size="1.4em" space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em" role="H4" id="ariaid-title114"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0"><fo:inline background-color="transparent" color="transparent" font-size="0px" max-width="2px" vertical-align="super" id="d689e17863"/><fo:inline background-color="transparent" color="transparent" font-size="0px" max-width="2px" vertical-align="super" id="d689e17867"/><fo:inline background-color="transparent" color="transparent" font-size="0px" max-width="2px" vertical-align="super" id="d689e17871"/><fo:inline>Scenario 1 — Generic Topic - No
                                                Dominant Classification Signal</fo:inline></fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                        
                                        <fo:block-container space-after="0" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">
                                            <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="0.5em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">A section titled "What's New
                                                in Version 4.2" has an introductory sentence and a
                                                bullet</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                            <fo:block-container space-after="1em" space-before="1em" role="Sect"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">
                                                <fo:block-container space-after="0.5em" margin-left="0" margin-right="0" space-before="1em"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0">A
                                                  section titled "What's New in Version 4.2" has an
                                                  introductory sentence and a bullet list of
                                                  features. The heading contains no classification
                                                  keyword, and the body does not contain any
                                                  numbered list or table.</fo:block></fo:block-container>
                                                <fo:block>
                                                  <fo:table-and-caption border-collapse="collapse" id="d689e17888" space-before="1em" space-after="1em"><fo:table-caption start-indent="0" end-indent="0" keep-with-next="always"><fo:block-container page-break-after="avoid" font-weight="bold" margin-top="0.5em" text-align="left"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0"><fo:inline>Table<fo:inline> 97</fo:inline><fo:inline>. </fo:inline></fo:inline><fo:inline><fo:inline>Generic topic, no clear
                                                  signal</fo:inline></fo:inline></fo:block></fo:block-container></fo:table-caption><fo:table-caption-for-next-page start-indent="0" end-indent="0" keep-with-next="always"><fo:block-container page-break-after="avoid" font-weight="bold" margin-top="0.5em" text-align="left"><fo:block end-indent="0" start-indent="0"><fo:inline>Table<fo:inline> 97</fo:inline><fo:inline>. </fo:inline></fo:inline><fo:inline><fo:inline>Generic topic, no clear
                                                  signal</fo:inline></fo:inline><fo:inline> (continued)</fo:inline></fo:block></fo:block-container></fo:table-caption-for-next-page><fo:table relative-align="baseline" chfox:html-table-width-policy="yes" table-layout="auto" border-bottom-color="black" border-bottom-style="solid" border-bottom-width="1px" border-left-color="black" border-left-style="solid" border-left-width="1px" margin-left="0" border-right-color="black" border-right-style="solid" border-right-width="1px" margin-right="0" border-top-color="black" border-top-style="solid" border-top-width="1px" hyphenate="true" space-before="0" space-after="0"><fo:table-column/><fo:table-column/><fo:table-header font-weight="bold" text-align="center" display-align="center">
